<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eadred</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 923–955</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Eadred of England</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eadred (c. 923–955) was king of the English from 946 to 955, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-the-elder">Edward the Elder</a> and younger brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelstan">Æthelstan</a> and Edmund. His reign was dominated by the struggle for York, where Northumbrian leaders accepted Norse kings such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eric-bloodaxe">Eric Bloodaxe</a>; in 948 he ravaged Northumbria and burned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ripon">Ripon</a>. After Eric's expulsion in 954 Northumbria was finally absorbed into the English kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eadred.jpg" alt="Eadred" width="320" height="293" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eadred_-_MS_Royal_14_B_VI.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
